## 7. Conclusion

Reliable authentication logging is a baseline control for protecting business systems. This investigation showed that a default build can leave remote access unmonitored, that the gap is cheap to close, and that detection queries must be tested before they are trusted. Applying the recommendations above gives a business earlier warning of unauthorised access attempts and the evidence needed to respond.

